      <Docs>
        <summary>
          <para>AF finished a passive scan without finding focus, and may restart scanning at any time.</para>
          <para>Only used by CONTINUOUS_* AF modes. This is a transient state, the camera device may skip reporting this state in capture result.</para>
          <para>LEGACY camera devices do not support this state. When a passive scan has finished, it will always go to PASSIVE_FOCUSED.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/hardware/camera2/CameraMetadata#CONTROL_AF_STATE_PASSIVE_UNFOCUSED" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.hardware.camera2.CameraMetadata.CONTROL_AF_STATE_PASSIVE_UNFOCUSED</code>.</a></format></para>
